Retrieving a Value From a Dictionary

Elements in a dictionary are unsorted. That is, there is no guaranteed order in how the elements exist inside the dictionary.
General format for retrieving value from dictionary: dictionary[key]

If key in the dictionary, associated value is returned, otherwise, KeyError exception is raised

You can test whether a key is in a dictionary using the in and not in operators. This can be useful to prevent KeyError exceptions.


fruit_counts = {
"apple": 4,
"banana": 2,
"cherry": 10
}

print(fruit_counts['apple'])

4



